KG42.register("source_edge_archive-e89cd2ebc27faede7318cc54",{"id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R009::E::v141-c-R009-E001","paper":"23-hierarchical_market_structure","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","rule_ref":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R009","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R009-E001","source":"execution.energy_trade","target":"pricing.local","type":"conditional_on","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R009-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R009-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-44ec202cc152796d","target":"KG31-589dd70d32471060","source_occurrence_id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R009::V::execution.energy_trade","target_occurrence_id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R009::V::pricing.local","source_unit_id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","target_unit_id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","omega":{"market_type":"LEM_DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"LA role 1: buying electricity from the WEM and selling the same volume to the DNEM. | LA role 2: purchasing electricity from the DNEM and selling the same volume to the WEM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"2ebe2525e4c20bc21e6338d0c44b3b65e3af3251fa885a58e99396c2ad05b2b6","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The LA's purchase from the WEM and equal-volume resale to the DNEM are conditional on the DNEM price exceeding the WEM bus LMP. Scope: LA role 1: buying electricity from the WEM and selling the same volume to the DNEM. Condition: The LMP at the LA's bus in the WEM is lower than the electricity price in the DNEM. The LA's purchase from the DNEM and equal-volume resale to the WEM are conditional on the DNEM clearing price being below the WEM bus LMP. Scope: LA role 2: purchasing electricity from the DNEM and selling the same volume to the WEM. Condition: The MCP in the DNEM is lower than the LMP at the LA's bus in the WEM.","target_definition":"The DNO, as local market coordinator, provides the DNEM market clearing price. Scope: DNEM in the proposed hierarchical WEM-DNEM electricity market.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"The LA's purchase from the WEM and equal-volume resale to the DNEM are conditional on the DNEM price exceeding the WEM bus LMP. Scope: LA role 1: buying electricity from the WEM and selling the same volume to the DNEM. Condition: The LMP at the LA's bus in the WEM is lower than the electricity price in the DNEM.","expression":"\\left( LMP'_{o} \u003c \\lambda_0 \\right) \\implies \\left( P_l^{imp} > 0 \\right), \\quad o \\in B_l^o","formalization_origin":"equivalent_translation","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R009-x001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R009-theta001","v141-c-R009-theta002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g01-E014","v141-b-g01-E015"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"The LA's purchase from the DNEM and equal-volume resale to the WEM are conditional on the DNEM clearing price being below the WEM bus LMP. Scope: LA role 2: purchasing electricity from the DNEM and selling the same volume to the WEM. Condition: The MCP in the DNEM is lower than the LMP at the LA's bus in the WEM.","expression":"\\left( \\lambda_0 \u003c LMP'_{o} \\right) \\implies \\left( P_l^{exp} > 0 \\right), \\quad o \\in B_l^o","formalization_origin":"equivalent_translation","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R009-x002"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R009-theta001","v141-c-R009-theta002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E014","v141-b-g01-E015"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E009","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"II-C LAs Objective","anchor_text":"MANSHADI AND KHODAYAR: HIERARCHICAL ELECTRICITY MARKET STRUCTURE electricity from the WEM and sell t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Each LA participates in the WEM and the DNEM. The LA acts as a broker playing two different roles: 1) buy electricity from the WEM and sell the same volume to the DNEM, if the LMP on the LAs bus in the WEM is lower than that in the DNEM; and 2) purchase electricity from the DNEM and sell the same volume to the WEM, if the MCP in the DNEM is lower than the LMP on the LAs bus in the WEM."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E010","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"II-C LAs Objective","anchor_text":"of providing electricity to the distribution network. The LAs bidding vector in the DNEM is given in","equation_id":"(7)-(9)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Considering role “1,” LA l maximizes the payoff function which is shown in (7), subjected to the bidding vector constraint (8). Here, LMP' is the marginal price of electricity on the LAs bus in the WEM which is determined as the cost of providing electricity to the distribution network. The LAs bidding vector in the DNEM is given in (9)\nR_l = \\max_{\\psi_l,P_l^{imp}} \\left[ \\left(\\lambda_0 - \\sum_{o\\in B_l^o} LMP'_o\\right) P_l^{imp} \\right] \\tag{7}\n\\underline{\\psi}_l \\le \\psi_l \\le \\bar{\\psi}_l \\tag{8}\n\\rho_l = \\psi_l * \\sum_{o\\in B_l^o} LMP'_o. \\tag{9}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E011","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"II-C LAs Objective","anchor_text":"of providing electricity to the distribution network. The LAs bidding vector in the DNEM is given in","equation_id":"(10)-(12)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"R'_l = \\max_{\\psi'_l,P_l^{exp}} \\left[ \\left(\\sum_{o\\in B_l^o} LMP'_o - \\lambda_0\\right) P_l^{exp} \\right] \\tag{10}\n\\underline{\\psi}'_l \\le \\psi'_l \\le \\bar{\\psi}'_l \\tag{11}\n\\rho'_l = \\psi'_l * \\lambda_0. \\tag{12}\nConsidering role “2,” the LA l maximizes the payoff function which is shown in (10), subjected to the constraints on the bidding vector (11). The MCP (\\lambda_0) in the DNEM is the marginal cost of providing electricity to the WEM. The bidding vector of LA l in the WEM is shown in (12)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E014","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"II-D WEM Clearing Process","anchor_text":"Fb ≤⎝ SFb.Pj + SFb.Pl ⎠ Th o∈Boj o∈Bol lev in , λ′− −SFob.PDo − SFob.Pimpl ≤¯Fb ∀b, λ′+b b in o∈Bol ","equation_id":"(18)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"As shown in (18), the Lagrangian multipliers associated with the load balance and transmission line capacity constraints are employed to calculate the LMPs on each bus in the WEM.\nLMP'_o = \\lambda'_0 + \\sum_b (SF_b^o)^T \\cdot (\\lambda_b^{'+} - \\lambda_b^{'-}). \\tag{18}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E015","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"II-E DNEM Clearing Process","anchor_text":"y As min ρm ∗Pm + ρl ∗Pimpl (19) m l 7) s.t. Pm + Pimpl = PD + Pexpl λ0 (20) m l l 8) P m ≤Pm ≤¯Pm ∀","equation_id":"(19)-(22)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The DNO minimizes the operational cost of distribution network as shown by\n\\min \\sum_m \\rho_m * P_m + \\sum_l \\rho_l * P_l^{imp} \\tag{19}\ns.t. \\sum_m P_m + \\sum_l P_l^{imp} = P^D + \\sum_l P_l^{exp} \\quad \\lambda_0 \\tag{20}\n\\underline{P}_m \\le P_m \\le \\bar{P}_m \\quad \\forall m \\tag{21}\n\\underline{P}_l^{imp} \\le P_l^{imp} \\le \\bar{P}_l^{imp} \\quad \\forall l. \\tag{22}\nThe load balance in the distribution network is shown in (20). The constraints on the awarded generation for microgrids and the imported power by the LA are shown in (21) and (22), respectively. Here, \\lambda_0 is the Lagrangian multiplier for the generation and load balance constraint in the distribution network as it is assumed that the electricity delivery is not limited by the line congestions."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM_DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"LA role 1: buying electricity from the WEM and selling the same volume to the DNEM. | LA role 2: purchasing electricity from the DNEM and selling the same volume to the WEM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R009-E001","source":"execution.energy_trade","target":"pricing.local","type":"conditional_on","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R009-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009"]},"paper_scope_note":"The interface between WEM and DNEM is retained; the two LA roles and the 15 MW revenue in Case 1 cannot be treated as general rules for the whole market."}});
